<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the bundle's generated Info.plist by tauri-bundler, which looks for
  a file of this name next to tauri.conf.json. Only the keys Tauri does not
  generate itself belong here.

  NSCameraUsageDescription is what makes "scatta e registra" possible in the
  desktop app at all. macOS does not DENY camera access to an app without it — it
  terminates the process, so its absence reads as a crash rather than as a refused
  permission. The string is shown verbatim in the system prompt, so it says what
  the camera is actually for.

  Deliberately NOT here: NSMicrophoneUsageDescription. The capture asks for
  `audio: false`, and declaring a permission that is never exercised would make
  macOS offer the user a choice about something the app does not do.

  Also not here, and needed only if this app is ever SIGNED with the hardened
  runtime (it is not today — .github/workflows/desktop-build.yml ships an unsigned
  DMG): the `com.apple.security.device.camera` entitlement, via
  bundle.macOS.entitlements. Adding it now would invoke codesign with an
  entitlements file and no identity, which fails instead of preparing anything.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
    <string>Ridley uses the camera to grab a view of the object on the registration plate and register it into the acquisition session.</string>
</dict>
</plist>
